     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "RAG (Repetitive Alphabets Generator) is a type of generative art project that creates and generates images using repetitive patterns of different alphabets. It was created by artist Robert Irwin in 1964 and has since become one of the most famous examples of generative art. RAG consists of a set of alphabets, each with a specific set of shapes or letters that are randomly generated based on certain rules. The resulting images are unique and dynamic, with a clear sense of repetition combined with unexpected juxtapositions of forms and colors.\n"
     ]
    }
